    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n# \n ![](https://huggingface.co/avatars/d75b66f764f129f39625c55034516a23.svg) ⟨28⟩\nakshatdev14⟨28⟩\n/\ndistilbert_intent_model⟨29⟩\nlike 1\n Text Classification ⟨30⟩ Transformers ⟨31⟩ Safetensors ⟨32⟩ distilbert ⟨33⟩ Generated from Trainer ⟨34⟩\nLicense: apache-2.0\n Model card ⟨29⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨35⟩ Community ⟨36⟩\nDeploy\nCopy to bucket new\nUse this model\n### Instructions to use akshatdev14/distilbert_intent_model with libraries, inference providers, notebooks, and local apps. Follow these links to get started.\n  * Libraries\n  *  Transformers⟨37⟩\nHow to use akshatdev14/distilbert_intent_model with Transformers:\n\n```\n# Use a pipeline as a high-level helper\nfrom transformers import pipeline\n\npipe = pipeline(\"text-classification\", model=\"akshatdev14/distilbert_intent_model\")\n```\n\n```\n# Load model directly\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForSequenceClassification\n\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"akshatdev14/distilbert_intent_model\")\nmodel = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(\"akshatdev14/distilbert_intent_model\", device_map=\"auto\")\n```\n\n  * Notebooks\n  *  Google Colab⟨38⟩\n  *  Kaggle⟨39⟩\n\n\n  * distilbert_intent_model⟨40⟩\n    * Model description⟨41⟩\n    * Intended uses & limitations⟨42⟩\n    * Training and evaluation data⟨43⟩\n    * Training procedure⟨44⟩\n      * Training hyperparameters⟨45⟩\n      * Training results⟨46⟩\n      * Framework versions⟨47⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨48⟩ distilbert_intent_model \nThis model is a fine-tuned version of distilbert-base-uncased⟨49⟩ on the None dataset. It achieves the following results on the evaluation set:\n  * Loss: 0.0363\n  * Accuracy: 0.9970\n\n\n##   ⟨41⟩ Model description \nMore information needed\n##   ⟨42⟩ Intended uses & limitations \nMore information needed\n##   ⟨43⟩ Training and evaluation data \nMore information needed\n##   ⟨44⟩ Training procedure \n###   ⟨45⟩ Training hyperparameters \nThe following hyperparameters were used during training:\n  * learning_rate: 2e-05\n  * train_batch_size: 64\n  * eval_batch_size: 64\n  * seed: 42\n  * optimizer: Use OptimizerNames.ADAMW_TORCH_FUSED with betas=(0.9,0.999) and epsilon=1e-08 and optimizer_args=No additional optimizer arguments\n  * lr_scheduler_type: linear\n  * num_epochs: 3\n  * mixed_precision_training: Native AMP\n\n\n###   ⟨46⟩ Training results   \n| Training Loss  | Epoch  | Step  | Validation Loss  | Accuracy  |  \n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |  \n| No log  | 1.0  | 336  | 0.2197  | 0.9927  |  \n| 1.7272  | 2.0  | 672  | 0.0480  | 0.9965  |  \n| 0.0529  | 3.0  | 1008  | 0.0363  | 0.9970  |  \n###   ⟨47⟩ Framework versions \n  * Transformers 5.0.0\n  * Pytorch 2.10.0+cu128\n  * Datasets 5.0.0\n  * Tokenizers 0.22.2\n\n\n\nDownloads last month\n    35\nSafetensors⟨50⟩\nModel size\n67M params\nTensor type\nF32 \n·\nFiles info\nInference Providers NEW⟨51⟩\n Text Classification ⟨52⟩\nThis model isn't deployed by any Inference Provider. 🙋 Ask for provider support⟨53⟩\n##  Model tree for akshatdev14/distilbert_intent_model ⟨54⟩\nBase model\ndistilbert/distilbert-base-uncased⟨55⟩\nFinetuned\n(12058⟨56⟩)\nthis model\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨57⟩ Privacy⟨58⟩ About⟨59⟩ Careers⟨60⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\nInference providers allow you to run inference using different serverless providers.\n",
